# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how to use the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") to implement quantum algorithms directly in fermionic space, rather than mapping to qubits first.\n"
msgstr "Ce guide explique comment utiliser [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") pour implémenter des algorithmes quantiques directement dans l'espace fermionique, au lieu de passer d'abord par un mapping vers des qubits.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use fermionic circuits {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "Pourquoi utiliser des circuits fermioniques {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the traditional workflow for implementing the time evolution of a fermionic Hamiltonian on a qubit-based architecture:\n"
msgstr "Considère le workflow traditionnel pour implémenter l'évolution temporelle d'un hamiltonien fermionique sur une architecture à base de qubits :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the fermionic Hamiltonian (for example, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"
msgstr "Définis le hamiltonien fermionique (par exemple, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map it to a qubit operator (for example, by using the Jordan-Wigner mapping).\n"
msgstr "Mappe-le vers un opérateur de qubits (par exemple, avec le mapping de Jordan-Wigner).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution in qubit space (using Trotterization or other methods).\n"
msgstr "Implémente l'évolution temporelle dans l'espace des qubits (avec la trotterisation ou d'autres méthodes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach has a fundamental limitation; early mapping to qubits discards problem-aware knowledge about the fermionic structure. Standard optimization passes cannot exploit fermionic symmetries or allowed term reorderings, resulting in suboptimal circuits with unnecessary depths and gate counts.\n"
msgstr "Cette approche a une limite fondamentale : le mapping précoce vers des qubits fait perdre les connaissances propres au problème sur la structure fermionique. Les passes d'optimisation standard ne peuvent pas exploiter les symétries fermioniques ni les réordonnancements de termes autorisés, ce qui produit des circuits sous-optimaux avec des profondeurs et des nombres de portes inutilement élevés.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") enables a better workflow:\n"
msgstr "[`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") permet un meilleur workflow :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution directly in fermionic space using fermionic gates.\n"
msgstr "Implémente l'évolution temporelle directement dans l'espace fermionique à l'aide de portes fermioniques.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map to qubit space as part of the transpilation process.\n"
msgstr "Effectue le mapping vers l'espace des qubits dans le cadre du processus de transpilation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach addresses the limitation by keeping problem-aware knowledge in fermionic space, where optimization passes can exploit fermionic structure and commutation relations to reduce circuit depth. The fermionic circuit describes what computation to perform, while transpilation handles how to map it to qubits, providing a cleaner separation of concerns.\n"
msgstr "Cette approche lève la limite en conservant les connaissances propres au problème dans l'espace fermionique, où les passes d'optimisation peuvent exploiter la structure fermionique et les relations de commutation pour réduire la profondeur du circuit. Le circuit fermionique décrit quel calcul effectuer, tandis que la transpilation gère comment le mapper vers des qubits, ce qui offre une séparation des responsabilités plus claire.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "Indexation générique des modes {#generic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both the [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") use generic mode-based indexing that makes no assumptions about the nature of the modes. A mode is simply an abstract index labeling a fermionic degree of freedom, with no inherent semantics. This design choice mirrors the operators module and ensures maximum flexibility. For example, you can implement time evolution for any operator implementing the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, regardless of its mathematical representation.\n"
msgstr "Le module [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") comme [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") utilisent une indexation générique par modes, qui ne fait aucune hypothèse sur la nature des modes. Un mode est simplement un indice abstrait qui désigne un degré de liberté fermionique, sans sémantique propre. Ce choix de conception reprend celui du module operators et garantit une flexibilité maximale. Par exemple, tu peux implémenter l'évolution temporelle de n'importe quel opérateur qui implémente le protocole [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\"), quelle que soit sa représentation mathématique.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a fermionic circuit {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "Construire un circuit fermionique {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below implements the time evolution described in the previous section. It constructs a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") by specifying the number of fermionic modes, then adds fermionic gates from the [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") to implement the time evolution.\n"
msgstr "L'exemple ci-dessous implémente l'évolution temporelle décrite dans la section précédente. Il construit un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") en indiquant le nombre de modes fermioniques, puis ajoute des portes fermioniques issues de [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") pour implémenter l'évolution temporelle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example also demonstrates how to incorporate domain knowledge into an operator by using [operator term grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation). By assigning group indices to the Hamiltonian terms, you preserve structural information that optimization passes can exploit throughout the transpilation stack.\n"
msgstr "L'exemple montre aussi comment intégrer des connaissances du domaine dans un opérateur grâce au [regroupement des termes de l'opérateur](grouping#grouping-explanation). En attribuant des indices de groupe aux termes du hamiltonien, tu conserves une information structurelle que les passes d'optimisation peuvent exploiter dans toute la pile de transpilation.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice how the operator term grouping is preserved even in simple operations like decomposition. This demonstrates how structural information flows through the circuit stack. To understand the full transpilation to qubits, refer to the [Transpiling fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Remarque que le regroupement des termes de l'opérateur est préservé même lors d'opérations simples comme la décomposition. Cela montre comment l'information structurelle circule dans la pile de circuits. Pour comprendre la transpilation complète vers des qubits, consulte le guide [Transpiler des circuits fermioniques](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep gates apart with a barrier {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"
msgstr "Séparer des portes avec une barrière {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimization passes fuse neighboring gates where they can. For example, [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines a run of consecutive [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates into one, and [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") folds an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") into the rotation that follows it.\n"
msgstr "Les passes d'optimisation fusionnent les portes voisines lorsque c'est possible. Par exemple, [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combine une suite de portes [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") consécutives en une seule, et [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") intègre une porte [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") dans la rotation qui la suit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") when you want to prevent that. A barrier carries no unitary effect, so it does not change the state your circuit prepares; it only marks a point that the passes do not fuse across. Call it without arguments to span every mode, or pass the modes to restrict it to:\n"
msgstr "Utilise [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") quand tu veux l'empêcher. Une barrière n'a aucun effet unitaire, donc elle ne change pas l'état que prépare ton circuit ; elle marque seulement un point que les passes ne fusionnent pas. Appelle-la sans argument pour couvrir tous les modes, ou passe les modes auxquels la restreindre :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers survive the fermion-to-qubit transpilation, so they also constrain the qubit-level optimization that follows. The [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide covers that stage.\n"
msgstr "Les barrières survivent à la transpilation fermion-vers-qubit, donc elles contraignent aussi l'optimisation au niveau des qubits qui suit. Le guide [Transpiler des circuits fermioniques](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) couvre cette étape.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"
msgstr "Répéter un circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many algorithms apply the same block of gates many times over. Time evolution is the common case: a Trotter step is built once, then repeated to reach the target time. Use [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") to build the repeated circuit, and [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") to join it to a state preparation prefix.\n"
msgstr "De nombreux algorithmes appliquent un même bloc de portes de nombreuses fois. L'évolution temporelle en est le cas courant : un pas de Trotter est construit une fois, puis répété pour atteindre le temps cible. Utilise [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") pour construire le circuit répété, et [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") pour l'attacher à un préfixe de préparation d'état.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below builds a second-order Trotter step for a Fermi-Hubbard model. The step is symmetric: it splits the hopping term into two half-duration [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates surrounding the on-site interaction.\n"
msgstr "L'exemple ci-dessous construit un pas de Trotter d'ordre deux pour un modèle de Fermi-Hubbard. Le pas est symétrique : il sépare le terme de saut en deux portes [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") de demi-durée qui encadrent l'interaction sur site.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeating the step and composing it onto a Hartree-Fock reference gives the full evolution:\n"
msgstr "Répéter le pas et le composer sur une référence de Hartree-Fock donne l'évolution complète :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The repetitions are flattened into the returned circuit rather than wrapped in a single gate, so [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") counts two rotations per step. That flattening is what makes the redundancy at the step boundaries visible to the transpiler: the trailing half-duration rotation of one step and the leading one of the next are adjacent, so [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines them into a single rotation.\n"
msgstr "Les répétitions sont aplaties dans le circuit retourné au lieu d'être enveloppées dans une seule porte, donc [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") compte deux rotations par pas. Cet aplatissement rend visible pour le transpileur la redondance aux frontières des pas : la rotation de demi-durée finale d'un pas et la rotation initiale du suivant sont adjacentes, donc [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") les combine en une seule rotation.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result costs one rotation per step plus one, which is what you get by fusing those half-steps by hand. Writing the step in its natural symmetric form and repeating it produces the same circuit, so the fusion is left to the optimization stage.\n"
msgstr "Le résultat coûte une rotation par pas plus une, ce qui correspond à ce que tu obtiens en fusionnant ces demi-pas à la main. Écrire le pas sous sa forme symétrique naturelle et le répéter produit le même circuit, donc la fusion est laissée à l'étape d'optimisation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you need the repetitions kept apart, pass `insert_barriers=True` to place a [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") between them. The optimization passes do not fuse gates across a barrier, so every rotation survives:\n"
msgstr "Quand tu as besoin de garder les répétitions séparées, passe `insert_barriers=True` pour placer une [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") entre elles. Les passes d'optimisation ne fusionnent pas les portes de part et d'autre d'une barrière, donc chaque rotation subsiste :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `reps` argument of [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") is a different concept. It subdivides a single [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate into more, shorter factors, whereas [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") duplicates whole circuits. Repeating a circuit that holds one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") only multiplies its total evolution time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Remarque\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  L'argument `reps` de [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") est un concept différent. Il subdivise une seule porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") en facteurs plus nombreux et plus courts, alors que [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") duplique des circuits entiers. Répéter un circuit qui contient une seule [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ne fait que multiplier son temps d'évolution total.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure fermionic modes {#measure-fermionic-modes}"
msgstr "Mesurer des modes fermioniques {#measure-fermionic-modes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") reads every mode out into a classical bit of its own, pairing mode `i` with bit `i`. Use [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") with your own [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) to read out only some of them.\n"
msgstr "[`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") lit chaque mode dans un bit classique distinct, en associant le mode `i` au bit `i`. Utilise [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") avec ton propre [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) pour n'en lire que certains.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `inplace=False` returns a measured copy and leaves the original alone, which matters because a measurement is not unitary: a circuit carrying one can no longer be applied to a state vector, so keep an unmeasured circuit around if you also want to simulate it.\n"
msgstr "Passer `inplace=False` retourne une copie mesurée et laisse l'original intact, ce qui compte car une mesure n'est pas unitaire : un circuit qui en contient une ne peut plus être appliqué à un vecteur d'état, donc garde un circuit non mesuré si tu veux aussi le simuler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring here, rather than on the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), is what keeps the sampled bitstrings easy to read. A fermionic measurement names the mode it reads, so every stage that moves modes around ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") at the fermionic level, layout and routing at the qubit level) carries the measurement along with it, and the bitstring stays indexed by the mode you asked about.\n"
msgstr "Mesurer ici, plutôt que sur le [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) transpilé, permet de garder les chaînes de bits échantillonnées faciles à lire. Une mesure fermionique nomme le mode qu'elle lit, donc chaque étape qui déplace des modes ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") au niveau fermionique, placement et routage au niveau des qubits) emporte la mesure avec elle, et la chaîne de bits reste indexée par le mode que tu as demandé.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Unlike [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), no [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") is inserted before the measurements. Call [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") yourself first if you want one there.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Remarque\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Contrairement à [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), aucune [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") n'est insérée avant les mesures. Appelle d'abord [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") toi-même si tu en veux une à cet endroit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Whether a measured bit means what you expect depends on the fermion-to-qubit encoding, which is chosen during transpilation rather than here. Under an occupation-basis encoding such as Jordan-Wigner each mode is carried by one qubit and the bit is that mode’s occupation; see [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Que le bit mesuré signifie ce que tu attends dépend de l'encodage fermion-vers-qubit, qui est choisi pendant la transpilation et non ici. Avec un encodage en base d'occupation comme Jordan-Wigner, chaque mode est porté par un qubit et le bit est l'occupation de ce mode ; consulte [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile fermionic circuits {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "Transpiler des circuits fermioniques {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To implement the quantum algorithm represented by your [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") it must be transpiled to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). You can learn how to do this in the [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Pour implémenter l'algorithme quantique représenté par ton [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\"), il doit être transpilé en un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Tu peux apprendre comment faire dans le guide [Transpiler des circuits fermioniques](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

